  "text": "Worldwide, hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) is one of the leading causes of cancer-related deaths[48]; in China, HCC is the fourth most common cancer and the third leading cause of cancer-related death[1]. Despite diagnostic and therapeutic advancements, disease relapse limits HCC survival rates, as recurrent tumors respond poorly to chemotherapy[2]. Therefore, identifying new therapeutic targets for HCC is necessary, as, in contrast with other solid tumors such as breast, colon and melanoma, an important hallmark of HCC is the absence of clear oncogene addiction[3–5]."
